  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nCurrently, the dimensions of an &lt;area&gt; element's clickable region are all set in CSS pixels.\nThis breaks down when the image is no longer shown at its original size, due to something like `max-width`. Now all the areas are at the wrong scale, since they are still just the same amount of CSS pixels away from the top left corner of the image.\nIt would make sense to stretch and squash the area element's regions to responsively stay in sync with the image as it is actually drawn.\n\nIdeally, this should also take CSS `object-fit` into account.",
